<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://ilc.cnr.it/klab/ontology/cooccurrence-measures#"
     xml:base="https://ilc.cnr.it/klab/ontology/cooccurrence-measures"
     xmlns:dct="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:collscore="https://ilc.cnr.it/klab/ontology/cooccurrence-measures#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://ilc.cnr.it/klab/ontology/cooccurrence-measures">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://ilc.cnr.it/klab/ontology/cooccurrence-measures/1.1.0"/>
        <dct:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-10</dct:created>
        <dct:description xml:lang="en">Unofficial, standalone OWL vocabulary for the ontological
    representation of the eleven co-occurrence association measures
    discussed in the DSH manuscript &apos;Dalla co-occorrenza alla
    collocazione&apos;. Developed to address the current lack of a
    dedicated ontological vocabulary systematically describing
    these measures, it defines measure-specific score properties
    as specializations (rdfs:subPropertyOf) of the general
    OntoLex-FrAC property frac:cScore. Each measure is documented
    through its definition, calculation formula, statistical
    assumptions, and verified scientific references. The vocabulary
    is neither an extension of LexInfo nor an official W3C
    OntoLex vocabulary.</dct:description>
        <dct:description xml:lang="it">Vocabolario OWL autonomo e non ufficiale per la rappresentazione
    ontologica delle undici misure di associazione delle co-occorrenze
    discusse nel manoscritto DSH &apos;Dalla co-occorrenza alla
    collocazione&apos;. Il vocabolario nasce per colmare l&apos;attuale
    mancanza di una descrizione ontologica sistematica di tali misure
    e definisce proprietà specifiche per ciascuna misura come
    specializzazioni (rdfs:subPropertyOf) della proprietà generale
    frac:cScore di OntoLex-FrAC. Ogni misura è documentata attraverso
    la propria definizione, la formula di calcolo, le assunzioni
    statistiche e i riferimenti scientifici verificati.
    Il vocabolario non costituisce un&apos;estensione di LexInfo
    né una specifica ufficiale W3C OntoLex.</dct:description>
        <dct:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-10</dct:modified>
        <dct:source rdf:resource="https://ontolex.github.io/frequency-attestation-corpus-information/"/>
        <dct:title xml:lang="en">Co-occurrence Statistical Measures Ontology</dct:title>
        <dct:title xml:lang="it">Ontologia delle misure statistiche di co-occorrenza</dct:title>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">OWL 2 DL modeling choice: each metric is represented by TWO DIFFERENT IRIs: an owl:NamedIndividual of cstat:CooccurrenceMeasure (e.g. collscore:LogDice), and an owl:DatatypeProperty for recording a numeric result (e.g. collscore:logDice). The two are linked bidirectionally with annotation properties collscore:denotesMeasure and collscore:scoreProperty. These are metadata links (queryable in RDF/SPARQL), not OWL object-property axioms; no punning is used.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="it">Scelta di modellazione OWL 2 DL: ogni misura e&apos; rappresentata da DUE IRI DISTINTI, un owl:NamedIndividual (es. collscore:LogDice) e una owl:DatatypeProperty (es. collscore:logDice). I due termini sono collegati dalle proprieta&apos; di annotazione collscore:denotesMeasure e collscore:scoreProperty, interrogabili in RDF/SPARQL. Non si utilizza il punning.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://aclanthology.org/2022.gwll-1.3/"/>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.1.0</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


